# Trivy vuln-scan suppressions for the audit-deps pre-commit hook.
# One CVE per entry; state why it's safe to ignore and when to revisit.

# langchain-core 0.3.86: path traversal in legacy load_prompt()/
# load_prompt_from_config() (langchain_core.prompts.loading). Not called
# anywhere in this codebase (grep for `load_prompt` across app/backend
# returns nothing) — unreachable in this app. Fixed only in 1.2.22, which
# requires langchain>=... langchain-core<1.0.0 to be dropped; both pinned
# sprig-side packages (langchain==0.3.30, langchain-community==0.3.27,
# see app/backend/requirements.txt:51-56) require langchain-core<1.0.0 on
# PyPI, so bumping breaks the RAG/sprig stack. Revisit when the sprig-side
# langchain stack is upgraded past 0.3.x as a coordinated major bump
# (tracked in TODO.md, Repo Hygiene & Security).
CVE-2026-34070
